  "label": "intended audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed for an audience that may be familiar with or receptive to racist tropes, particularly those involving anti-Black stereotypes. The target community likely includes individuals who either consciously or unconsciously endorse or are indifferent to the dehumanizing metaphor of equating Black people with enslaved Africans and animals (like ants). The meme’s intent is to normalize or justify racial prejudice, so its target audience may be those who are already exposed to or sympathetic to such hateful content, or who are seeking to provoke or reinforce racist ideologies through humor or shock value. The visual of black ants and the text 'some of my best slaves are black' are specifically crafted to appeal to those who understand the historical reference to slavery and the dehumanizing stereotype of comparing Black people to primates or animals, making the target audience likely to be individuals who are either unaware of the harm or who actively engage with such content as a form of dark humor or social commentary.",
